description: |
    The new ``jira`` exporter creates and updates Jira Cloud issues from
    resolved tmt metadata. It targets the Red Hat Jira instance with a
    ``Test Case`` issue type, the ``ID`` UUID field, the ``URL`` automation
    field and the ``Active`` workflow status. Public enrichment and
    post-export hooks support site-specific integrations. The exporter
    prepares and validates the whole collection before writes; dry-run
    output displays planned fields and operations. Existing UUIDs are
    preserved, ambiguous identities and collisions are rejected, and
    contact resolution handles display names and email ambiguity.

    Use ``--create`` to allow creation and ``--dry`` to preview without
    writes. Metadata backlinks require ``--link-jira``; ``--bugzilla``
    recreates Bugzilla ``verifies`` links as remote links and ``--polarion``
    stores the Polarion case URL. See :ref:`jira-project-configuration` for
    authentication, schema requirements and extension examples.

    .. code-block:: shell

        tmt tests export --how jira --create --link-jira \
            --jira-url https://issues.redhat.com \
            --jira-user me@example.com --jira-token TOKEN \
            --project-id RHELTEST
